# Documents UI Standard

This app is based on [Documents: Simple Next.js Documentation](https://vercel.com/templates/next.js/documents-simple-next-js-documentation) (rubix-documents). Preserve that docs-site look. Do not invent a new visual language.

Before changing UI, load the project `shadcn` skill (`.agents/skills/shadcn` / `.cursor/skills/shadcn`) and reuse existing primitives.

## Layout shells (do not collapse)

| Route | Shell |
| --- | --- |
| `/` | Centered sections under root Navbar/Footer — no sidebar/TOC |
| `/docs/*`, `/companies/*` | Left Sidebar + article + right TOC (`xl+`) |
| `/resume/*` | Wide centered editorial page — no sidebar/TOC |

Root chrome: `Navbar` + `main.px-5.sm:px-8` + `Footer` in `app/layout.tsx`.

## Visual tokens

- Theme source: `styles/globals.css` (zinc / oklch semantic tokens). Default theme is **light**.
- Colors: only semantic classes — `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-muted`, `bg-accent`. No `gray-*` / ad-hoc hex for chrome.
- Type: Inter + Noto Sans SC. Prefer `font-semibold` + `tracking-tight` for titles; avoid `font-bold` unless matching an existing control.
- Density: docs use `gap-10`, sticky `top-26`; home kickers use `text-xs tracking-[0.22em] text-muted-foreground uppercase`.
- Surfaces: prefer borders/dividers over shadows. Cards (`rounded-xl border bg-card`) only where home heatmap/roadmap already use them — not in docs article body by default.
- Controls: use `@/components/ui/*` and `buttonVariants`. Add via `npx shadcn@latest add …`, do not hand-roll duplicates.

## Article callouts

Callouts inside MDX (`<Note>`, `<MyQuestion>`) are the one place hue colors are allowed — pick the color by what the box says, never for looks. Styles live in `components/markdown/callout.ts`; don't restyle a callout inline.

| Color | Component | Content |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Gray | `<Note>` (default) | Supplementary context, term distinctions, background — optional reading |
| Green | `<Note type="tip">` | Connections to other mechanisms or classic behaviors; points worth raising unprompted in an interview |
| Orange | `<Note type="warning">` | Pitfalls — easy to misunderstand, likely follow-up questions |
| Red | `<Note type="danger">` | Wrong claims — saying this in an interview costs you |
| Blue | `<MyQuestion q="…">` | The learner's own questions and answers; collapsed by default |

All callouts share the same box: left accent bar, icon, colored title, `my-8` so stacked callouts stay visibly separate.

## Canonical files to match

1. `styles/globals.css`
2. `components/navigation/navbar.tsx`, `footer.tsx`, `logo.tsx`
3. `components/ui/button.tsx`
4. `app/[collection]/layout.tsx`, `app/[collection]/[[...slug]]/page.tsx`
5. `components/article/*`, `components/sidebar/*`, `components/toc/*`
6. Home-only: `components/home/*` — resume-only: `components/resume/*`

## Anti-patterns

- Purple/indigo gradients, glow, glassmorphism, cream+terracotta, broadsheet newspaper layouts
- Replacing docs three-column shell with dashboards/card grids
- Raw `<button>` / `<input>` when shadcn equivalents exist
- Nested card stacks, pill clusters, stat strips on docs pages
- Mixing resume editorial layout into docs, or docs sidebar into home/resume

## When asked to "improve UI"

Extend the current shell and tokens. Match spacing/typography of the nearest sibling page. Ask before changing global theme, fonts, or layout architecture.
